WHEN ADVERTISING NETWORKS INTO BGP, BGP WILL ONLY ADVERTISE NETWORKS, WHOSE EXACT PREFIX AND SUBNET MASK APPEARS IN THE ROUTING TABLE

SOLUTION: WE NEED TO CONFIGURE A DISCARD ROUTE POINTING NOWHERE - STATIC ROUTE GOING TO ADVERTISED NETWORK ADDR POINTING NOWHERE, 
THE PURPOSE IS TO PUSH YOUR ROUTER TO PUT THAT ROUTE IN THE ROUTING TABLE

DISCARD ROUTE SYNTAX:
conf t
ip  route  <net addr>  <subnet mask>  null0
exit

CREATE A DISCARD ROUTE FOR 185.32.40.80/29 ON E1

E1:
